  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (2S)-2-Amino-4-((carboxycarbonyl)amino)butanoic acid may act as a target for SMMC-7721 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links the compound to Caspase-6, which is then targeted by 4,5-Di-O-methyl-8-prenylafzelechin-4beta-ol, ultimately targeting SMMC-7721. The second pathway connects the compound to Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2, which is targeted by 15-Dehydroxythyrsenol A, also leading to SMMC-7721. Both pathways involve targets that are known to interact with cancer cells, suggesting a potential role in oncogenic processes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which the compound may influence SMMC-7721, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a role in oncology, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
